    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "The question states oxygen concentrations and OMZ thresholds in micromoles per kilogram, while this fragment says CMIP6/OMIP BGC tracers are stored per unit volume and observational products are per unit mass, so a density-based unit conversion is required.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Before the 20 and 60 µmol kg-1 thresholds are applied, convert `o2` from mol m-3 with an in-situ density (`compute_potential_density_anomaly`, `ref_pressure=None`); `transform_unit`'s constant surface-density default errs ~1 % in the deep ocean — state `attrs['density_assumption']`.",
        "For the global oxygen inventory use the native mol m-3 field with `convert_concentration_to_content` (Σ c·volcello needs no density); multiplying by 1000 and labelling the result \"µmol/kg\" is a mistake."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "CMIP6 files mark land and below-sea-floor cells with 1e20, which must be masked before summing volumes or inventories or those values will dominate the results.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "1e20 is the CMIP6 fill; use NaN-aware reductions with weights masked to the same valid cells, and treat any output near 1e20 or 9.97e36 as an unmasked fill value.",
        "Build each field's valid mask from the field itself (masks differ between variables of the same model); `compute_exceedance_fraction` keeps land out of numerator and denominator, while a hand-written threshold test counts NaN as False (land in the denominator)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "Comparing model OMZ thickness maps and volumes with WOA23, and ranking which model reproduces the observed OMZ, requires a shared ocean mask because the fragment says comparisons exist only where both fields have data.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put all fields on one grid, build one mask with `build_comparison_mask` and apply `.where(mask)` to every field before multi-source metrics; `ocean_only=True` (default) is right here because WOA23 is part of the comparison.",
        "Report the cell counts the mask records alongside the metrics; a mask much smaller than the fields means the products disagree about where the ocean is."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen.md",
      "sha256": "afe46747641c91aff8ddc9f50165a800a7c64d5d2e39b50e816280d02e59fba3",
      "reason": "The question asks for WOA23 apparent oxygen utilization and percent oxygen saturation inside the OMZ, and this fragment defines the o2sat/AOU/saturation relationships and warns that observational and model units/formulas differ.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "AOU = `o2sat` − `o2` and percent saturation = 100·`o2`/`o2sat` are consistent per model (same grid, member, volume basis; the basis cancels in percent saturation but not in AOU); convert to µmol kg-1 before comparing with WOA23 AOU.",
        "Model and WOA23 saturation values may rest on different solubility conventions and pressure assumptions; state that the AOU and percent-saturation differences include a definitional component."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The question asks for Pacific, Indian and Atlantic OMZ volumes using a basin mask, and this fragment says basin statistics depend on the chosen partition and must state it.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Basin volumes use the WOA23 mask via `select_basin`/`load_basin_mask` with `include_marginal_seas=True` (the question's \"marginal seas folded into their parent ocean\"); state that this is WOA labelling, not the OMIP 10-region mask.",
        "Use `depth_dependent=False` (surface labels applied through the column) for a named ocean; each level's own labels (`depth_dependent=True`) are what a water-mass analysis wants."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "OMZ volume and total dissolved oxygen inventory are integrals requiring volume weighting or summation over all grid points in the region, as this fragment specifies.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Volume means/integrals are Σ x·volcello / Σ volcello over valid cells only (`compute_basic_stat`, `op='volume_weighted_mean'`); the weight must be restricted to the same cells as the data, never land.",
        "`compute_exceedance_fraction` returns the volume behind a percentage with missing cells out of the denominator; the mean of a cell-by-cell ratio is not the ratio of the means — state which one is reported."
      ]
    },
    {
